/// Diagnostics and quoting this file's `printf` shares with other builtins:
/// an invalid number names its argument's bytes as they are (`read -n`,
/// `pushd`, `popd`, `ulimit`), and `$'…'` quoting takes glibc's printable
/// characters (`${v@Q}`, `declare -p`, `%q`).
